# --------------------- supplementary observation (not the prescribed break) ---------------------
#
# The prescribed edit to "=26.10.2" fails before cargo compares the lock: 26.10.2 is not a
# published heif-rs version (the registry lists 26.10.3, 26.10.1, 26.10.0, ...), so the
# resolver refuses with "failed to select a version" above. To show the --locked lock-file
# refusal the spec predicts, the same requirement edit was repeated against 26.10.1, which
# does resolve; the lock still says 26.10.3, so --locked refuses instead of rewriting it.

$ sed -i 's/^heif-rs = "=26.10.3"$/heif-rs = "=26.10.1"/' src-tauri/Cargo.toml
#   after: 24:heif-rs = "=26.10.1"

$ scripts/ci.sh rust
