# Observation: the two cargo failures differ because of what the registry can supply.
#   A nonexistent version (=26.10.2) is refused by the resolver. An existing but wrong
#   version (=26.10.1) resolves and is then refused by --locked, which is the check the spec
#   assigns to the Rust gate. Neither edit touched Cargo.lock. With the manifest restored,
#   the build finishes from the existing target/ and exits 0.
